Cthulhu: remove Firefox View at the source and put the Home tab in its place.

WHAT THIS DOES
  * browser.js               FirefoxViewHandler's body is replaced with the Home
                             tab implementation. The NAME is kept on purpose:
                             ~25 call sites across SessionStore, tabbrowser,
                             the all-tabs menu and URILoadingHelper compare
                             against FirefoxViewHandler.tab; with .tab
                             permanently null they are all inert, so the Home
                             tab is an ordinary pinned tab everywhere and none
                             of them need patching. Every former Firefox View
                             entry point (openTab / openToolbarMouseEvent) now
                             toggles Home. Also enforces, at this level:
                               - the Home tab can never be navigated away in
                                 place (loads are reopened in a new tab);
                               - dropping a tab on the button pins it.
  * browser-init.js          Calls FirefoxViewHandler.init() from
                             _delayedStartup. Upstream defined init() but never
                             called it anywhere.
  * navigator-toolbox.inc.xhtml
                             The button is relabelled with the existing
                             navbar-home string. Its id is unchanged so
                             CustomizableUI placement, tabs.css [open] styling
                             and the toolbar migration keep working.
  * browser-menubar.inc.xhtml / browser-menubar.js / nonbrowser-mac.js
                             Tools > Firefox View menu item removed.
  * QuickActionsLoaderDefault.sys.mjs
                             "Firefox View" urlbar quick action removed.
  * AboutRedirector.cpp / components.conf
                             about:firefoxview unregistered.

WHAT IT DELIBERATELY LEAVES
  browser/components/firefoxview/ stays in the build. The Sidebar's history,
  bookmarks and synced-tabs panels, split view and the AI window all import
  helpers.mjs / fxview-tab-list.mjs / firefoxview.css from that directory.
  With about:firefoxview gone it is an internal library, not a feature.

The visual side (icon, hiding the pinned Home tab from the strip) lives in
src/theme/content/browser.css. Regenerate after an ESR bump with
tools/rebase-esr.sh; the hunks are small except browser.js.

